A||||10||JetroGT||Refinishing My Rims||||6||
Z||000000||JetroGT||05-12-2001||05:41 AM||||After a couple weeks of sanding and stripping paint I have my first rim done!<BR>First I started out with the unfinished product.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Raw.jpg"> <P>Then I went from 400 to 600 then 1500 grit silicon carbide sand paper. I did this all by hand so it was pain...literally!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Stripped_1.jpg"> <P>Then after masking the whole thing off I sprayed it with Rust-oleum semi-gloss enamel. I like the way it came out. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Refinished.jpg"> <P>Only three more to go...<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/JetroGTsig.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Oreif||05-12-2001||09:56 AM||||Looking good! That is how I refinished my wheels too. I don't know if you like the silver center caps, But Rodney sells black ones which also look good. It's just a matter of preference. So which ever way you like them, here's a pic of mine in case you want to compare.<BR>I agree sanding them by hand is a B*tch! But they do look nice. Also since you went down to 1500 grit, If you use Mother's Aluminum polish, The outside ring will look like chrome.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheel_5.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||deceler8||05-12-2001||10:20 AM||||Three words on refinishing rims...<P>Black & Decker Mouse.<P>Did a set from start to finish including clear coating them in less than three hours.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||05-13-2001||02:23 AM||||Oreif, I do have thoughs stick on caps. But their in gold insted of black. I'll set one on to see if they look good or not. <P>I think I'll have to get a electric sander of some kind. To get the paint out of the little holes in the lace wheels I was using some old socks. After the paint was softened up from  the stripper I just ran the sock through the rim. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||05-13-2001||10:06 PM||||I really like how mine came out too.  I didnt clear coat them for fear of chipping, but they get really dirty too easily.  I think I may end up getting some c/c and shooting them sometime soon when I get a chance.<P>some pics within: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005246.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005246.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||05-13-2001||11:40 PM||||Looks great man!<P>What'd you use to strip them?||||reg||1
Z||000006||JetroGT||05-14-2001||01:38 AM||||I just used Citra Strip. I had to use it a few times to get all of the paint off. A stronger stripper would probably work better. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||05-14-2001||09:32 AM||||To get the paint out of the lace (and to strip the rest of the wheel easier) I used Permatex spray-on Gasket Remover. The stuff works so much better than the "paint stripper" products. Just spray it on and in about 15 minutes just brush it off with a brass detail brush. (looks like a brass toothbrush, Brash won't mark up the aluminum)<BR>I was able to strip all 4 wheels in about 2 hours.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Will||05-14-2001||01:17 PM||||I was thinking about sand blasting and clear powder coating one of my sets of lace wheels. Any thoughts on this, anyone?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero5||05-14-2001||01:24 PM||||I looked into getting a set of rims sandblasted and such afew years ago, and it was expensive!<P>It seems that just doing them yourself is cheaper and looks just about as good.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero3_3.jpg">       <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||4
Z||000010||terryk||05-14-2001||05:57 PM||||If you've ever tried sand or bead blast powdercoat off, you'll have more success using your tonque.<P>I finally had to use a combo of stripper and blasting. And more stripper. And more stripper....||||reg||1
